  "expected_demo_result": "failed",
  "notes": "Deliberately ZERO-MARGIN twin of v1: same planner, but it spends the WHOLE frustum (sweep_coverage_gain 1.0, no cone overlap) and parks exactly on the keep-out radius (standoff_margin_cm 0.0). It is GREEN on all 16 scenarios at the 'nominal' domain -- it is geometrically correct, just with nothing in reserve -- and GREEN under 'actuation_degraded' (it is in fact cheaper than v1, using fewer gazes). Under 'obs_noise' it goes RED on 14 of 16 scenarios: 7 on coverage_complete (2.0 deg of aim error pushes an end target past the 12 deg cone, e.g. worst_target_gap 12.42 deg on visible row 0) and 7 on standoff_respected (the +x component of the perception error parks the head 0.09-2.69 cm INSIDE the keep-out). Kept as the honest red half of the perception behavior's red/green history."
}
